@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Credits";
}

<article class="aa-legal mx-auto">
    <header class="aa-legal-head">
        <span class="aa-eyebrow">Thank you</span>
        <h1 class="aa-section-title">Credits</h1>
        <p class="lead mb-0">Academia Auditiva is also made of work that other people share freely. Here is where our sounds and fonts come from.</p>
    </header>

    <section id="sounds">
        <h2>Instrument sounds</h2>
        <p>The guitar and the violin you can pick in the exercises come from the <strong>FluidR3_GM</strong> SoundFont by Frank Wen (© 2000–2002, 2008, MIT License), as rendered note by note by Benjamin Gleitzman's <a href="https://github.com/gleitz/midi-js-soundfonts">midi-js-soundfonts</a> project (© 2012, MIT License). These renderings are shared under the <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/us/">Creative Commons Attribution 3.0</a> license.</p>
        <p class="mb-0">We changed them: every note was mixed down to mono, its loudness matched to our piano, and encoded again. The violin rendering has no sound for its highest notes (A#6 and F#7 to B7), so we made those by resampling the nearest violin note below. The full license notices are in our <a href="https://github.com/lcarli/AcademiaAuditiva/blob/master/AcademiaAuditiva/Audio/Instruments/LICENSE.txt">source code</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="fonts">
        <h2>Fonts</h2>
        <ul class="mb-0">
            <li><strong>Inter</strong>, © 2016 The Inter Project Authors, under the <a href="~/fonts/Inter-OFL.txt">SIL Open Font License 1.1</a>.</li>
            <li><strong>Fraunces</strong>, © 2020 The Fraunces Project Authors, under the <a href="~/fonts/Fraunces-OFL.txt">SIL Open Font License 1.1</a>.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>
</article>
